The team wants to set up Agent Platform Model Monitoring on a deployed online prediction endpoint to detect feature distribution skew. A team member writes the following Python configuration.

```python
from google.cloud import aiplatform_v1

monitoring_config = aiplatform_v1.ModelDeploymentMonitoringJob(
    display_name='fraud-monitoring',
    endpoint='projects/proj/locations/us-central1/endpoints/EP_ID',
    model_deployment_monitoring_objective_configs=[
        aiplatform_v1.ModelDeploymentMonitoringObjectiveConfig(
            deployed_model_id='MODEL_ID',
            objective_config=aiplatform_v1.ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfig(
                training_dataset=aiplatform_v1.ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfig.TrainingDataset(
                    bigquery_source=aiplatform_v1.BigQuerySource(
                        input_uri='bq://project.dataset.training_table'
                    )
                ),
                training_prediction_skew_detection_config=aiplatform_v1.
                    ModelMonitoringObjectiveConfig.TrainingPredictionSkewDetectionConfig(
                        skew_thresholds={'age': aiplatform_v1.ThresholdConfig(value=0.1)}
                    )
            )
        )
    ],
    logging_sampling_fraction=0.1
)
```

What does `logging_sampling_fraction=0.1` control in this monitoring configuration?

The team is configuring drift detection for a production fraud model. The serving data is logged to BigQuery, and they want to detect when the distribution of the age feature drifts significantly from the training distribution. A team member writes the following drift configuration.

